{"id":"8e66cb31cc497cdd405028527334646ba8c785cb","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/airavata","sha":"8e66cb31cc497cdd405028527334646ba8c785cb","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"cmd/airavata-mcp/main.go","lines":["@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@ Usage:"," "," Every flag can also be set with the environment variable shown in its help."," The token can be given in AIRAVATA_MCP_TOKEN instead of logging in; it is never a flag.","+Accepts both CILogon and Airavata service account tokens."," `"," "," func main() {"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/api.md","lines":["@@ -47,6 +47,53 @@ The statuses in use:"," "," Internal failures return `500` with a fixed `\"Internal server error\"` message: the underlying detail is logged rather than returned, since it may name internal state."," ","+## Users","+","+Airavata tracks user accounts created via identity providers (CILogon), administrator registration, or service accounts.","+","+### Read Current User","+","+```","+GET /api/v1/users/me","+```","+","+Returns the authenticated caller's own identity, permissions, and user record. Available to any signed-in user or service account.","+","+**curl example**","+","+```bash","+TOKEN='<a user or service account token>'","+","+curl -s localhost:9095/api/v1/users/me \\","+  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"","+```","+","+**Response — `200 OK`**","+","+```json","+{","+  \"userId\": \"sa:pipeline-worker\",","+  \"status\": \"ACTIVE\",","+  \"authorities\": [],","+  \"permissions\": [],","+  \"admin\": false,","+  \"user\": {","+    \"userId\": \"sa:pipeline-worker\",","+    \"status\": \"ACTIVE\",","+    \"firstName\": \"Pipeline Worker\",","+    \"lastName\": null,","+    \"email\": \"worker@example.org\",","+    \"authMethod\": \"SERVICE_ACCOUNT\",","+    \"roles\": [],","+    \"createdAt\": 1755043200000","+  }","+}","+```","+","+| Status | Meaning |","+|---|---|","+| `401 Unauthorized` | no token, or invalid/expired token |","+"," ## SSH Credentials"," "," An SSH credential is a registered keypair, and it belongs to whoever registered it. Registering one is self-service — any authenticated caller may — but nothing about it is reachable by anyone else: reading, updating and deleting a credential are the owner's alone, and the listing returns only the caller's own."],"additions":47,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/auth.md","lines":["@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ An expired, regenerated-away or disabled token gets `401` with `WWW-Authenticate"," "," `GET /api/v1/service-accounts` lists all service accounts and `GET /api/v1/service-accounts/{id}` reads one. Neither returns a token. Use `tokenExpiresAt` (milliseconds since the epoch) to find tokens that need renewing."," ","-[airavata-mcp](mcp.md) signs in through CILogon only, so service account tokens can't be used with it.","+[airavata-mcp](mcp.md) accepts service account tokens via the `AIRAVATA_MCP_TOKEN` environment variable, validating them directly against the Airavata server."," "," ### Root account"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/mcp.md","lines":["@@ -19,9 +19,10 @@ bin/airavata-mcp login --device   # on an SSH session or HPC login node"," ```"," "," The access and refresh tokens are stored in the OS keychain and refreshed automatically. `airavata-mcp logout`","-removes them. For CI you can set `AIRAVATA_MCP_TOKEN` instead; it is never a flag, so it never shows up in a","-process listing, and it cannot be refreshed. Airavata's bootstrap root token is refused: every token's identity","-is checked with the issuer's userinfo endpoint.","+removes them. For CI, automated runs, or background agents you can set `AIRAVATA_MCP_TOKEN` instead (supporting both","+personal CILogon tokens and Airavata service account tokens prefixed with `airavata_sa_`); it is never a flag, so","+it never shows up in a process listing, and it cannot be refreshed. Service account tokens are validated directly","+against `airavata-server` and run with `USER` authority. Airavata's bootstrap root token is refused."," "," ## Connect a client"," ","@@ -40,7 +41,7 @@ Every flag has an environment variable; a flag wins over its variable."," | Flag | Environment variable | Default | |"," |---|---|---|---|"," | `--api-url` | `AIRAVATA_MCP_API_URL` | `http://localhost:9095` | `airavata-server` base URL |","-| (none) | `AIRAVATA_MCP_TOKEN` | | Overrides the keychain token |","+| (none) | `AIRAVATA_MCP_TOKEN` | | Overrides the keychain token (supports CILogon and service account tokens) |"," | `--oauth-issuer` | `AIRAVATA_MCP_OAUTH_ISSUER` | `https://cilogon.org` | OpenID Connect issuer used by `login` |"," | `--oauth-client-id` | `AIRAVATA_MCP_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` | | Public client id used by `login` |"," | `--allow-write` / `--read-only` | `AIRAVATA_MCP_ALLOW_WRITE` | read-only | Write tools are not even listed without it |"],"additions":5,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"internal/mcp/auth/auth.go","lines":["@@ -148,6 +148,9 @@ func (d *discovery) oauth(cfg Config, redirect string) *oauth2.Config {"," }"," "," func Identify(ctx context.Context, cfg Config, accessToken string) (*Principal, error) {","+\tif srvauth.IsServiceAccountToken(accessToken) {","+\t\treturn identifyServiceAccount(ctx, cfg, accessToken)","+\t}"," \tcfg, err := cfg.withDefaults()"," \tif err != nil {"," \t\treturn nil, err","@@ -159,6 +162,66 @@ func Identify(ctx context.Context, cfg Config, accessToken string) (*Principal,"," \treturn identify(ctx, cfg, d, accessToken)"," }"," ","+func identifyServiceAccount(ctx context.Context, cfg Config, accessToken string) (*Principal, error) {","+\tif cfg.HTTPClient == nil {","+\t\tcfg.HTTPClient = &http.Client{Timeout: 30 * time.Second}","+\t}","+\tapiURL := strings.TrimRight(cfg.APIURL, \"/\")","+\tif apiURL == \"\" {","+\t\tapiURL = \"http://localhost:9095\"","+\t}","+\tu := apiURL + \"/api/v1/users/me\"","+\treq, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, http.MethodGet, u, nil)","+\tif err != nil {","+\t\treturn nil, err","+\t}","+\